The Lobster is a 2015 absurdist black comedy-drama art film directed and co-produced by
Yorgos Lanthimos, from a screenplay by Lanthimos and Efthimis Filippou.

11
00:54:32,500 --> 00:54:38,500
It stars Colin Farrell, Rachel Weisz, Jessica Barden, Olivia Colman,
Ashley Jensen, Ariane Labed, Angeliki Papoulia, John C.

12
00:59:30,000 --> 00:59:36,000
Reilly, Léa Seydoux, Michael Smiley, and Ben Whishaw.

13
01:04:27,500 --> 01:04:33,500
The film follows a newly single bachelor who moves into a hotel with other singles, who are all obliged to
find a romantic partner within 45 days; otherwise, they’ll be transformed into animals.

14
01:09:25,000 --> 01:09:31,000
The film was announced in October 2013, with Jason
Clarke originally cast in the lead role.

15
01:14:22,500 --> 01:14:28,500
After Clarke left production, Farrell replaced him by February 2014, with
Weisz also joining the cast after Elizabeth Olsen dropped out.

16
01:19:20,000 --> 01:19:26,000
The rest of the cast was rounded out by March as principal
photography began, which concluded in May.

17
01:24:17,500 --> 01:24:23,500
Filming largely took place in Dublin and County Kerry.

18
01:29:15,000 --> 01:29:21,000
The film is a co-production by Ireland, the United
Kingdom, Greece, France, and the Netherlands.

19
01:34:12,500 --> 01:34:18,500
The Lobster premiered at the 2015 Cannes Film Festival on 15 May, where
it competed for the Palme d'Or and won the Jury Prize.

20
01:39:10,000 --> 01:39:16,000
It was theatrically released in the United Kingdom on 16 October
2015, grossing $18 million on a $4 million budget.

21
01:44:07,500 --> 01:44:13,500
The film received positive reviews from critics, with praise for its screenplay, humor, originality, and thematic content, and was nominated for
Best Original Screenplay at the 89th Academy Awards and for Outstanding British Film at the 69th British Academy Film Awards.

22
01:49:05,000 --> 01:49:11,000
The film explores themes of hotel, suicide attempt, boat, dystopia, woods.

23
01:54:02,500 --> 01:54:08,500
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
